values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i082$il$, $il$Cannot send LinkedIn messages. Send fails unauthorized, same as AI edit$il$, $il$Outreach & drafting$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$blocker$il$, $il$done$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-16T10:01:50.000Z'::timestamptz, 0, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], $il$Brad$il$, '2026-09-18T10:44:17.835Z'::timestamptz, false, false, $il${"Brad": "2026-09-18T07:53:04.206Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$BLOCKER. Press Send now on an approved draft and it returns: Send failed: unauthorized. Try again or send manually from LinkedIn. Nothing goes out.

READ THIS WITH i070. AI edit fails with unauthorized. Send fails with unauthorized. Same word, two different functions, on the same day. They are almost certainly one fault, not two, and fixing them as one thing will be faster than chasing them separately.

THE PATTERN SO FAR: reads work. The page loads, drafts render, the guards evaluate, the lint scores. What fails is anything that ACTS: rewriting a draft, sending a message. That points at the session token not reaching the functions that perform actions, rather than at the model or at LinkedIn.

It also means the review queue cannot drain at either end. Drafts cannot be corrected, and now they cannot be sent. 74 were waiting yesterday with one message sent.$il$,
$il$THE FASTEST TRIAGE, in order:
1. Does Regenerate work? It was the question on i070 and it now splits three ways rather than two. If Regenerate works but AI edit and Send both fail, the model credential is fine and it is the action routes. If Regenerate also fails, everything that calls out is failing and it is one credential or one token.
2. Does a reload fix it? If an expired session shows up as unauthorized instead of asking Oliver to sign in again, then the session handling is the bug and the two symptoms are just where it surfaces.
3. Is it every draft or some? Same question as i070, and the answers should match. If they do not, they really are two bugs.

THE FALLBACK IN THE MESSAGE IS THE DANGEROUS PART. Try again or send manually from LinkedIn is sensible advice and it quietly breaks the record: a message sent by hand in LinkedIn is a touch that Lovable did not write. That is i048 and i052, and the four hourly watcher should catch it, but only for DMs. So if Oliver works around this for a few days, expect gaps. Worth confirming the watcher backfills anything sent manually during the outage, and worth saying so in the toast.

CHASER 3 OF 2, VISIBLE ON THE SAME SCREEN, is a separate defect and it is evidence for i053. The footer reads logged as chaser 3 of 2. A sequence cannot be at position three of two. i053 predicted exactly this: a duplicated touch row makes the sequence think it is a step further along than it is. That is no longer a theory, it is on screen.

THE GUARDS ARE WORKING WELL, again worth saying. On this draft they read: do not restate the Garantieverlaengerung wedge or the 4-5x figure, both already spent; no question mark anywhere in the message; no meeting, call or estimate offer; do not mention that this is a third message or reference the prior touches. That is the exit message doctrine applied correctly and automatically, which is the hard part and it is done.$il$);
