values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i084$il$, $il$A draft broke its own guardrail and still scored LINT 100$il$, $il$Outreach & drafting$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-16T10:04:19.000Z'::timestamptz, 4, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$On the Robert Karl draft, guardrail one reads: do not lead with Pier Protect's own attachment rate stats or the 4-5x multiple, this is discovery not pitch.

The draft contains: Wir helfen Partnern das 4-5 Fache.

The lint score reads 100.

So the guardrails are being generated and displayed, and then not checked against the text. A score of 100 currently means the message was written, not that it passed anything.

That matters more than one bad draft. Oliver is being asked to review at volume, and a score that looks like a pass but is not one is worse than no score, because it invites approval. Either the lint evaluates every displayed guardrail, or the number should not be shown.$il$,
$il$HOW IT SHOULD BEHAVE: each guardrail is a check with a pass or fail against the current text, re-run on every edit and regeneration. The score is the count that passed. A failing guardrail turns red on the card and blocks Approve until it is resolved or explicitly overridden with a reason, the same override pattern as i055.

THE HARD PART IS THAT THESE ARE SEMANTIC, NOT STRING MATCHES. Do not use a hard meeting ask cannot be checked with a regular expression. But the two on this card that were broken are the easy kind: the 4-5x multiple is a literal, and a question mark rule is a literal. Do the literal ones as real lint now, and route the semantic ones to a model check. Partial enforcement that is honest about which rules it actually tested beats a single number that implies all of them.

SHOW WHAT WAS CHECKED. If the score covers four of seven guardrails, say four of seven. That is the same argument as i061, why this message was written: a number with no visible basis gets trusted until it fails badly once, and then it never gets trusted again.

TWO MORE THINGS ON THE SAME DRAFT. It signs off Oli, which is i067 again and now three sightings. And the body appears to stop mid sentence, at Wir helfen Partnern das 4-5 Fache, with the sign off directly after. Worth confirming whether that is the real content or the textarea cropping in the screenshot, because a truncated send is a different and worse bug.$il$);
