$il$17 Sept, SECOND UPDATE, AND IT CORRECTS PART OF THIS ITEM. The WeFix draft to Louis Salzman-Le Goff scores LINT 85, not 100, and shows a real failure underneath the draft in red: Use Partner not client. So the lint IS evaluating something and CAN score below 100. This item said a score of 100 currently means the message was written; that is too strong. What is true is that it checks some rules and not others, and gives no indication which.

THE SHARPER PROBLEM IS NOW VISIBLE. The rule failed, the failure is displayed, the draft still says clients twice, and Approve was available and worked. So a failing check does not block approval. That is exactly what this item asks for and there is now a screenshot of it not happening.

So the two asks separate cleanly. Evaluate every displayed guardrail, and say how many of them were actually tested. And make a failure block Approve until it is fixed or explicitly overridden with a reason.$il$
